/build/
# ...but build-support/ is the shared CMake kit an export of this product carries
# at its root. It only looks like a build directory (ADR 0011).
!/build-support/

# Golden-image scratch output. A failing comparison saves the render beside the
# tracked baseline as `testdata/actual_<name>.png` so it can be looked at, and
# scada_qt_golden_image.h encodes through `<name>.tmp.png` / `<name>.bak.png`
# siblings so a failed encode cannot truncate a baseline. None of them is a
# baseline, and leaving them untracked-but-not-ignored means a genuine
# rendering regression also leaves the tree dirty -- one `git add -A` away from
# committing a scratch render as if it were reviewed test data.
/testdata/actual_*
/testdata/*.tmp.*
/testdata/*.bak.*
